# settings-perfil: the real main screen with the firmware's real Ajustes window
# open, scrolled to the Appearance group, where the new "Visual profile" row lives
# (UI-08 incremento 5). The path is the firmware's own
# (main_screen_action(ACTION_APP_SETTINGS) -> dialog_construct -> dialog_settings.c)
# and the fixture jumps to the group exactly as the user does: `buttons_press(4)`
# loads page 2 through the "More >" button and `buttons_press(1)` presses its
# "Appearance" tab, which calls settings_goto() (scroll + focus). See src/screens.c
# (scenario_settle).
#
# The battery is 11.2 V without an external source, so the visual policy decides
# ECO on its own: the dropdown renders "Auto" (the persisted setting) while the
# row label reads "Visual profile (Eco)" (the effective/current profile). That is
# the point of the row — the state shown is the policy's, not only the setting's.
#
# Deterministic: the date/time fields read the harness' fixed clock, not the
# host's (tools/ui_harness/CMakeLists.txt links with `--wrap=time`).

name settings-perfil
screen settings-perfil

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 11.2
external_v 0
battery_cap 50
charging false

rxtx rx
